\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The overall framework of the proposed TLQLDMR model. Source domain (normal weather) and target domain (extreme weather) data are mapped into a high-dimensional RKHS via kernel mapping. The joint optimization objective integrates structural risk, distribution variance, MMD-based domain adaptation, and weighted pinball loss. The model outputs probabilistic prediction intervals for robust wind power forecasting under extreme conditions.}}{6}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{6}{The overall framework of the proposed TLQLDMR model. Source domain (normal weather) and target domain (extreme weather) data are mapped into a high-dimensional RKHS via kernel mapping. The joint optimization objective integrates structural risk, distribution variance, MMD-based domain adaptation, and weighted pinball loss. The model outputs probabilistic prediction intervals for robust wind power forecasting under extreme conditions}{figure.caption.1}{}}
